WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.600
Energy buffering, power sharing and load smoothing are related but different functions.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.620
A buffer stores energy and can supply or absorb power within its

3
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.360
permitted state and operating limits.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.900
The amount of energy and the duration of an event matter as

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.860
well as the peak power.

6
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.960
Power sharing redistributes demand or capacity within an architecture.

7
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.420
It doesn't create unlimited supply beyond the available system.

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.600
Load smoothing changes the demand presented at a selected boundary, but the

9
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.660
workload and storage still have to obey their own constraints.

10
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.520
For a proposed solution, name the event and the boundary it addresses.

11
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.360
A short buffer response may help with an excursion but cannot support

12
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.380
an indefinitely larger sustained load.

13
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:43.960
The relevant battery or capacitor system also requires its own qualification and

14
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:44.900
operating controls.

15
00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.920
We link the specialist storage course rather than treating a storage icon

16
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.760
as proof of safety or availability.

17
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.760
At rack level, verify that the function solves the stated problem and

18
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.540
that the complete response has evidence.

